      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "A sketch plan of Athens about 425. The agora was the town centre and market place, where the main civic buildings were. The assembly (ἐκκλησία) met on the hill of the Pnyx, and the Lykeion sports ground (γυμνάσιον) was a place for the men of the city to meet, exercise and discuss.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
